A||||0||GT Bastard||Just another kill story...  3.2 litre 86GT||||12||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||07-28-2000||11:49 PM||||A 3.2 stroker was recently transplanted into a friends purple '86 GT 4sp.  The mechanical work was done by another friend/fiero nut here in the city who drives a 3.1 '86SE.  It's basically a bottom end out of a 3.1 van with 2.8 goodies and a compucam 2030.  Anyhow, the bottom end already had 30,000 on it so he didn't have any problems with racing it a little.  We were both driving to Brads place at about 3am in the morning. Heading down a 4-lane, the GT pulls up along side me and starts provoking my lowly SE.  A couple car lengths behind me, he decides to nail it.  By the time I hit it, he's already at my back bumper so he got a jump on me from the start.  But by the time I shifted out of second gear, I walked away from him pretty nicely.  We both back off at about 90-100mph(this road is empty!) Talk about a rush...  He was mildly upset at losing to the SE, but was cool about it.  Luckily, my rod knock isn't any worse as a result(new block is being prepared for build-up to replace the tired stock unit.)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Gold 86 SE V6 4-sp w/4.10 gears, Eibach springs, Koni's all around w/some poly bushings<BR>Yoko's<BR>Coated headers<BR>ACT 4-puck clutch<BR>MSD ignition<BR>Flowmaster w/ mandrel bent 2.5 pipe<BR>extrude honed intake<BR>Lots of fuel system mods... etc etc...||||reg||12
